  "title": "Greek Euchologion 1754: complete Chrysostom anaphora constituent",
  "scope": "Complete Anaphora of the Liturgy of St John Chrysostom in the 1754 printing, as that book divides it: from the red deacon heading and Στῶμεν καλῶς (Printed p. 49 (provider PA49)) through the ekphonesis Καὶ δὸς ἡμῖν … τῶν αἰώνων that closes the intercessions (Printed p. 55 (provider PA55)), with every red heading, rubric, diaconal and choir line printed inside it and the footnote on the hierarch commemoration. 18 units, 120 reading lines. Excludes everything before Στῶμεν καλῶς and from Καὶ ἔσται τὰ ἐλέη onward. Neither the whole Divine Liturgy nor the whole book is claimed; whole-book text coverage remains partial.",
